{"id":"migdol","name":"Migdol","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:migdol"],"types":[],"standing":"single-index","indexes":["nave"],"thin":false,"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Migdol","text":"Tower. (1.) A strongly-fortified place 12 miles from Pelusium, in the north of Egypt (Jer. 44:1; 46:14). This word is rendered “tower” in Ezek. 29:10, but the margin correctly retains the name Migdol, “from Migdol to Syene;” i.e., from Migdol in the north to Syene in the south, in other words, the whole of Egypt. (2.) A place mentioned in the passage of the Red Sea (Ex. 14:2; Num. 33:7, 8). It is probably to be identified with Bir Suweis, about 2 miles from Suez."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H4024","lemma":"מִגְדּוֹל","xlit":"Migdôwl","gloss":"Migdol, a place in Egypt","kjv":"Migdol, tower","count":4,"share":0.8},{"strong":"H2583","lemma":"חָנָה","xlit":"chânâh","gloss":"to incline","kjv":"abide, camp, dwell, encamp","count":3,"share":0.6},{"strong":"H6440","lemma":"פָּנִים","xlit":"pânîym","gloss":"the face","kjv":"accept, a- fore, against, anger","count":3,"share":0.6}],"verses":["Exod.14.2","Num.33.7","Jer.44.1","Jer.46.14","Num.33.8"],"witnesses":["n","n","n","n","n"],"agreed":0,"broader":[],"narrower":[],"related":[{"id":"pi-hahiroth","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.5,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"baal-zephon","type":"lexical","strong":"H2583","why":"both lead with חָנָה (H2583)"},{"id":"etham","type":"lexical","strong":"H2583","why":"both lead with חָנָה (H2583)"},{"id":"oboth","type":"lexical","strong":"H2583","why":"both lead with חָנָה (H2583)"},{"id":"pi-hahiroth","type":"lexical","strong":"H2583","why":"both lead with חָנָה (H2583)"},{"id":"rephidim","type":"lexical","strong":"H2583","why":"both lead with חָנָה (H2583)"}],"works":[]}
